# Linked worktrees live here by convention — the directory name is the feature name, and that is
# what puts a row under `development` on the roadmap. They are checkouts, not content: never commit
# one into the repo that owns it.
worktrees/

# Every file this machinery writes goes down as a temp file and is then RENAMED over its target, so
# a kill mid-write cannot leave half a file. A kill BETWEEN the two steps leaves this debris, and
# debris must never become a finding in the check that reads the tree.
*.conducted-lite-tmp.*
